Third-party algorithm attribution
=================================

The complete component-to-paper and component-to-software mapping is in
inst/provenance/METHODS.md and its machine-readable companion methods.csv.
That inventory distinguishes a statistical-method reference, delegated
numerical fitting, and translated source code. Only the one-step implementation
described below is a source translation.

The one-step quantile-regression process implementation in R/solver_qr.R
is based on the algorithm and MIT-licensed Stata/Mata implementation in the
bmelly/Stata qrprocess project:

  https://github.com/bmelly/Stata
  https://github.com/bmelly/Stata/blob/main/qrprocess.ado

The public `onestep` point and bootstrap backends specifically transcribe
`rq_1step()` (source lines 2271-2359) and `rq_boot_1step()` (source lines
2362-2455) from qrprocess 1.1.3, frozen at commit:

  ec56830ef9c84ce54411ad59c5ce94535847d9df

The native R implementation uses R/quantreg numerical primitives in place of
Mata's exact solvers and `luinv()`. Algorithmic compatibility is intended;
cross-language bitwise identity is not claimed.

The Stata-compatible weighted-quantile helper follows the default type-2
definition documented and implemented by Ben Jann's MIT-licensed moremata
project:

  https://github.com/benjann/moremata

